---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How to Set Up WhatsApp Business Auto-Replies: A Complete Guide | LinkWA"
  description="Step-by-step tutorial to setting up auto-reply messages, away messages, and greeting messages on the WhatsApp Business App and API."
  canonical="https://linkwa.in/blog/whatsapp-business-auto-reply-setup"
>
<article class="article-wrap">
  <div class="article-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="article-tag">Guide</div>
      <h1>How to Set Up WhatsApp Business Auto-Replies</h1>
      <div class="article-meta"><span>Jun 22, 2026</span><span>·</span><span>5 min read</span></div>
      <p class="article-intro">Never keep a customer waiting. Here is how to configure greeting messages, away messages, and automated quick replies on WhatsApp Business to respond to leads instantly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="callout"><strong>Immediate responses:</strong> Over 80% of customers expect an immediate response when contacting a brand on messaging apps. Auto-replies ensure you never miss a lead.</div>

      <h2>Types of automated replies in WhatsApp Business</h2>
      <p>The standard WhatsApp Business application offers three types of native automation tools:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Greeting Messages:</strong> Sent automatically when a customer messages you for the first time or after 14 days of inactivity.</li>
        <li><strong>Away Messages:</strong> Sent during off-business hours to let customers know when you will be back online.</li>
        <li><strong>Quick Replies:</strong> Keyboard shortcuts for frequently sent templates (e.g. typing <code>/thanks</code> sends a full thank-you note).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Step-by-step: Setting up greeting messages</h2>
      <p>Welcome new prospects and set expectations immediately with a friendly greeting message:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open the WhatsApp Business app and tap <strong>Settings</strong> or <strong>Business Tools</strong>.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>Greeting message</strong>.</li>
        <li>Toggle <strong>Send greeting message</strong> on.</li>
        <li>Tap the edit icon to write your custom welcome message.</li>
        <li>Set the recipient list (e.g., "Everyone not in the address book" is recommended for businesses).</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Step-by-step: Configuring away messages</h2>
      <p>Let customers know your team is away so they don't look elsewhere for help:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Navigate to <strong>Business Tools</strong> and select <strong>Away message</strong>.</li>
        <li>Toggle <strong>Send away message</strong> on.</li>
        <li>Edit the text to include your business hours and when you will reply.</li>
        <li>Set the <strong>Schedule</strong> (e.g., "Outside of business hours" requires you to have configured your profile business hours).</li>
        <li>Select recipients and tap <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Best practices for automated WhatsApp messages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Be human:</strong> Use warm, conversational language. Avoid overly formal text.</li>
        <li><strong>Use formatting:</strong> Use bold (<code>*text*</code>), italics (<code>_text_</code>), and emojis to make your messages easy to read.</li>
        <li><strong>Provide alternative links:</strong> If you are away, include a link to your website, FAQ page, or product catalog.</li>
        <li><strong>Integrate custom links:</strong> Use LinkWA links with pre-filled keywords to trigger specific auto-replies based on what users click.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="article-cta">
      <h3>Enhance your customer entry points</h3>
      <p>Create dedicated WhatsApp links with pre-filled templates to make auto-replies work even better.</p>
      <a href="/" class="article-cta-btn">Open LinkWA →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="article-nav"><a href="/blog" class="back-link">← All articles</a></div>
  </div>
</article>
</Base>
